          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often knead when they feel safe, relaxed, or ready to settle down.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
          <span>Do indoor cats need regular playtime?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Yes. Daily play helps indoor cats exercise, practice natural hunting behaviors, and avoid boredom. Wand toys, puzzle feeders, and short chase games work well.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
